1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:18,630
Something that needs to always remain at the top of your mind is that for 350 years, this country's policies of who gets access to education, to resources, to health care, et cetera, was explicitly related to your race.

2
00:00:19,290 --> 00:00:23,130
It wasn't nuanced. It wasn't coded. It was explicit.

3
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:46,210
So when we acknowledge that, we have to acknowledge that on the other side of that, in the effort to actually treat Black Americans like the citizens they're supposed to be treated as in the 14th Amendment, there must be specific programs that are the antithesis of the specific legislation that there was to hold Black people back.

4
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:59,970
So to suggest that this Freedom Fund for Black women is somehow discriminatory or oppressive is to suggest that the entire nation's efforts for 350 years weren't the same.

